# Product bar

- BATorrent is a **shipping product** (thousands of users), not a study or school repo.
- Tracked repo contents must look like **professional shipping software**.
- Personal learning notes, curricula, and “things I don’t understand” belong only in
  gitignored `internal/` (or entirely out of tree) — never under tracked `docs/` or
  product `.cursor/rules/`. Agents may read `internal/LEARNING_PATH.md` when present
  for mentoring context; that file is not product documentation.
- Quality work and refactors serve **product stability and craft**. Learning may
  happen in parallel; it must never become the public artifact.
